<div class=3DWordSection1 style=3D'layout-grid:15.6pt'>

<p class=3DMsoNormal align=3Dcenter style=3D'text-align:center'><b><span la=
ng=3DEN-US
style=3D'font-size:18.0pt;line-height:115%'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><span class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDSH</sp=
an> Team<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal align=3Dcenter style=3D'text-align:center'><span lang=
=3DEN-US>User
Guide</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>## Table of Contents</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- [1. Installation </span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- [2. Platform Login</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- [3. Management Page</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- [4. DSH Workbench</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- [5. Member Work</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- [6. DSH Operation</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'text-indent:22.0pt;mso-char-indent-count:2.0'=
><span
lang=3DEN-US>This guide is intended for end users and clearly explains the =
entire
process: Installation </span>=A1=FA<span lang=3DEN-US> Login </span>=A1=FA<=
span lang=3DEN-US>
Opening the Workspace </span>=A1=FA<span lang=3DEN-US> File Management / My=
 Tasks </span>=A1=FA<span
lang=3DEN-US> Admin Task Assignment, Instance Management, Language Switchin=
g </span>=A1=FA<span
lang=3DEN-US> Member DSH Usage*<span class=3DGramE>*.</span></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>I. Installation</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'text-indent:33.0pt;mso-char-indent-count:3.0'=
><span
class=3DSpellE><span lang=3DEN-US>TakeTopDSH</span></span><span lang=3DEN-U=
S> Team is
a portable software that requires no installation</span>=A1=AA<span lang=3D=
EN-US>just
copy and use. Follow these steps: Copy the `<span class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDsh=
Team</span>`
folder to the target machine </span>=A1=FA<span lang=3DEN-US> On Windows, d=
ouble-click
`start.bat` , On macOS/Linux, run `./start.sh<span class=3DGramE>` <span
lang=3DEN-US><span lang=3DEN-US>=A1=FA </span></span></span>Open your brows=
er and go to
`<span class=3DGramE>http://127.0.0.1:46001` <span lang=3DEN-US><span lang=
=3DEN-US>=A1=FA </span></span></span>Click
**&quot;Open DSH&quot;** to start using it. Detailed instructions are as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>1-1 Windows</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-1-1. Copy the entire `<span
class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDshTeam</span>` folder to the target computer.</span>=
</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span class=3DGramE><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1</span></spa=
n><span
lang=3DEN-US>-1-2. Double-click **`start.bat`*<span class=3DGramE>* (</span=
>or
right-click </span>=A1=FA<span lang=3DEN-US> select &quot;Run as administra=
tor&quot;
if the port is occupied).</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-1-3. The browser will automatic=
ally
open the login page at `http://127.0.0.1:46001`.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>1-2 macOS (Apple Silicon, arm64)</s=
pan></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-2-1. Copy the entire `<span
class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDshTeam</span>` folder to the target Mac.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-2-2. Open Terminal, navigate to=
 the
folder:</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&n=
bsp;
</span>bash cd /path/to/<span class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDshTeam</span> <span
class=3DSpellE>chmod</span> +x start.sh./start.sh</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-2-3. On first run, it will
automatically extract Node and install `@deepseek-ai/dsh` (**requires an
internet connection once**).</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-2-4. The browser will automatic=
ally
open the login page at `http://127.0.0.1:46001`.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>1-3 Linux (x64 / arm<span class=3DG=
ramE>64)*</span>*</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-3-1. Copy the entire `<span
class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDshTeam</span>` folder to the target machine.</span><=
/p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-3-2. Open Terminal, navigate to=
 the
folder:</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&n=
bsp;
</span>bash cd /path/to/<span class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDshTeam</span> <span
class=3DSpellE>chmod</span> +x start.sh./start.sh</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-3-3. On first run, it automatic=
ally
extracts Node (**already bundled, no download required**); only native
dependencies for `@deepseek-ai/dsh` need **one-time online installation**,
after which it works offline.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>- 1-3-4. The browser will automatic=
ally
open the login page at `http://127.0.0.1:46001`.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-US>2. Platform Login</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'text-indent:22.0pt;mso-char-indent-count:2.0'=
><span
lang=3DEN-US>Each time you restart your computer, open the&nbsp;<span
class=3DSpellE>TakeTopDshTeam</span>&nbsp;folder. Inside, you will see the
following two files. Run the appropriate file for your operating system to =
open
the login page.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'text-indent:22.0pt;mso-char-indent-count:2.0'=
><span
